Subject: [PATCH] mpegts: probe the payload of streams labelled MPEG-1 audio

Some muxers label other audio, DTS among them, with stream type 0x03.
Taken at its word, the stream opens as MP3 and never decodes. The payload
is now probed, as it already is for 0x04 and AAC; a real MPEG audio stream
settles on its first packet.
---
 libavformat/mpegts.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/mpegts.c b/libavformat/mpegts.c
index 8ba6998..69501d5 100644
--- a/libavformat/mpegts.c
+++ b/libavformat/mpegts.c
@@ -955,7 +955,10 @@ static int mpegts_set_stream_info(AVStream *st, PESContext *pes,
     st->codecpar->codec_tag = pes->stream_type;
 
     mpegts_find_stream_type(st, pes->stream_type, ISO_types);
-    if (pes->stream_type == STREAM_TYPE_AUDIO_MPEG2 || pes->stream_type == STREAM_TYPE_AUDIO_AAC)
+    /* Some muxers label other audio (DTS among them) as MPEG-1 audio, so
+     * that label is confirmed by probing the payload like the two below. */
+    if (pes->stream_type == STREAM_TYPE_AUDIO_MPEG1 ||
+        pes->stream_type == STREAM_TYPE_AUDIO_MPEG2 || pes->stream_type == STREAM_TYPE_AUDIO_AAC)
         sti->request_probe = 50;
     if (pes->stream_type == STREAM_TYPE_PRIVATE_DATA)
         sti->request_probe = AVPROBE_SCORE_STREAM_RETRY;
